C1-8A C2-7A C6-3A 7.50 C7-6 8.00 C1-8X C2-7X C6-3D C6-3X 9.00 C1-8 C1-9 C2-7 C2-8 C4-6 C4-7 C4-9 C5-1 C5-2 C5-4 C6-3 C6-4 C6-5 C6-8 C7-7 10.00 C4-11 C6-11 C7-8 12.00 C4-12 C5-3 C5-5 C6-6 C6-7 C6-9 C6-12 C7-9 15.00"},{"id":"zr-17724-block-005","kind":"html","html":"<p><span>For <strong><em>zoning lots</em></strong> containing both <strong><em>commercial</em></strong> <strong><em>uses</em></strong> and <strong><em>community facility</em></strong> <strong><em>uses</em></strong>, the total <strong><em>floor area</em></strong> used for <strong><em>commercial</em></strong> <strong><em>uses</em></strong> shall not exceed the amount permitted for <strong><em>zoning lots</em></strong> containing only <strong><em>commercial</em></strong> <strong><em>uses</em></strong> in Section 33-122.</span></p>","plainText":"For zoning lots containing both commercial uses and community facility uses, the total floor area used for commercial uses shall not exceed the amount permitted for zoning lots containing only commercial uses in Section 33-122."},{"id":"zr-17724-block-006","kind":"html","html":"<p><span>In addition, the following provisions shall apply:</span></p>","plainText":"In addition, the following provisions shall apply:"},{"id":"zr-17724-block-007","kind":"html","html":"<p class=\"pseudo-li\" style=\"margin-left: 43pt;text-indent: -43pt;\"><span>(a)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;In C1 through C6 Districts, except districts with a <strong><em>residential equivalent</em></strong> of R10, R11 or R12 Districts, for any <strong><em>zoning lot</em></strong> containing philanthropic or non-profit institutions with sleeping accommodations, the total <strong><em>floor area</em></strong> used for such <strong><em>community facility</em></strong> <strong><em>use</em></strong> shall not exceed the amount as set forth in paragraphs (b) or (c) of Section <a class=\"sec-link-inline\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://zr.planning.nyc.gov/article-ii/chapter-4#24-111\" data-permitext-zr-source=\"https://zr.planning.nyc.gov/article-ii/chapter-4#24-111\"><span>24-111</span></a> (Maximum floor area ratio for certain community facility uses) applying the equivalent <strong><em>Residence District</em></strong> as specified in Section <a class=\"sec-link-inline\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://zr.planning.nyc.gov/article-iii/chapter-4#34-112\" data-permitext-zr-source=\"https://zr.planning.nyc.gov/article-iii/chapter-4#34-112\"><span>34-112</span></a> (Residential bulk regulations in other C1 or C2 Districts or in C3, C4, C5 or C6 Districts)&nbsp;for the <strong><em>Commercial District</em></strong> in which such <strong><em>use</em></strong> is located, unless modified pursuant to Section <a class=\"sec-link-inline\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://zr.planning.nyc.gov/article-vii/chapter-4#74-903\" data-permitext-zr-source=\"https://zr.planning.nyc.gov/article-vii/chapter-4#74-903\"><span>74-903</span></a> (Certain community facility uses in R3 to R9 Districts and certain Commercial Districts).</span></p>","plainText":"(a) In C1 through C6 Districts, except districts with a residential equivalent of R10, R11 or R12 Districts, for any zoning lot containing philanthropic or non-profit institutions with sleeping accommodations, the total floor area used for such community facility use shall not exceed the amount as set forth in paragraphs (b) or (c) of Section 24-111 (Maximum floor area ratio for certain community facility uses) applying the equivalent Residence District as specified in Section 34-112 (Residential bulk regulations in other C1 or C2 Districts or in C3, C4, C5 or C6 Districts) for the Commercial District in which such use is located, unless modified pursuant to Section 74-903 (Certain community facility uses in R3 to R9 Districts and certain Commercial Districts)."},{"id":"zr-17724-block-008","kind":"html","html":"<p class=\"pseudo-li\" style=\"margin-left: 43pt;text-indent: -43pt;\"><span>(b)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;The maximum <strong><em>floor area ratio</em></strong> for any <strong><em>zoning lot</em></strong> used partly for <strong><em>commercial</em></strong> <strong><em>use</em></strong> and partly for philanthropic or non-profit institutions with sleeping accommodations in C1 through C6 Districts, except districts with a <strong><em>residential equivalent</em></strong> of R10, R11 or R12 Districts, shall not exceed the amount permitted for a <strong><em>zoning lot</em></strong> containing <strong><em>commercial</em></strong> <strong><em>uses</em></strong> by the applicable district regulations. However, for the districts in which the allowable <strong><em>floor area ratio</em></strong>, as set forth in paragraphs (b) or (c) of Section <a class=\"sec-link-inline\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://zr.planning.nyc.gov/article-ii/chapter-4#24-111\" data-permitext-zr-source=\"https://zr.planning.nyc.gov/article-ii/chapter-4#24-111\"><span>24-111</span></a> exceeds the amount permitted for a <strong><em>zoning lot</em></strong> containing <strong><em>commercial</em></strong> <strong><em>uses</em></strong>, the provisions of paragraph (b) or (c) of Section <a class=\"sec-link-inline\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://zr.planning.nyc.gov/article-ii/chapter-4#24-111\" data-permitext-zr-source=\"https://zr.planning.nyc.gov/article-ii/chapter-4#24-111\"><span>24-111</span></a>, as applicable, shall be used to compute the maximum <strong><em>floor area</em></strong> permissible for the <strong><em>zoning lot</em></strong> unless modified pursuant to Section <a class=\"sec-link-inline\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://zr.planning.nyc.gov/article-vii/chapter-4#74-903\" data-permitext-zr-source=\"https://zr.planning.nyc.gov/article-vii/chapter-4#74-903\"><span>74-903</span></a>.</span></p>","plainText":"(b) The maximum floor area ratio for any zoning lot used partly for commercial use and partly for philanthropic or non-profit institutions with sleeping accommodations in C1 through C6 Districts, except districts with a residential equivalent of R10, R11 or R12 Districts, shall not exceed the amount permitted for a zoning lot containing commercial uses by the applicable district regulations. However, for the districts in which the allowable floor area ratio, as set forth in paragraphs (b) or (c) of Section 24-111 exceeds the amount permitted for a zoning lot containing commercial uses, the provisions of paragraph (b) or (c) of Section 24-111, as applicable, shall be used to compute the maximum floor area permissible for the zoning lot unless modified pursuant to Section 74-903."},{"id":"zr-17724-block-009","kind":"html","html":"<p style=\"margin-left: 43pt;text-indent: -43pt;\">&nbsp;</p>","plainText":""}],"zoning":{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceNodeID":17724,"sourcePath":"/article-iii/chapter-3/33-123","sourceURL":"https://zr.planning.nyc.gov/article-iii/chapter-3/33-123","sourceContentHash":"95aff951b6b3b347bb3c136704d5bff9b1764a3847745c9a9e24064e7c23fe4b","article":{"roman":"III","title":"Commercial District Regulations"},"chapter":{"number":"3","title":"Bulk Regulations for Commercial or Community Facility Buildings in Commercial Districts","canonicalNumber":"III-3"},"appendix":null,"subsections":[{"id":"zr-17724-sub-0b76cd95afa60025","label":"1.00","sourceAnchor":null,"plainText":"1.00","ordinal":0},{"id":"zr-17724-sub-ec060a77b2cae7c8","label":"2.00","sourceAnchor":null,"plainText":"2.00","ordinal":1},{"id":"zr-17724-sub-34c0d6d071c600d0","label":"2.40","sourceAnchor":null,"plainText":"2.40","ordinal":2},{"id":"zr-17724-sub-6cdae841446e6ab8","label":"3.00","sourceAnchor":null,"plainText":"3.00","ordinal":3},{"id":"zr-17724-sub-d856afe045df2a81","label":"4.00","sourceAnchor":null,"plainText":"4.00","ordinal":4},{"id":"zr-17724-sub-1641a430605617ec","label":"4.20","sourceAnchor":null,"plainText":"4.20","ordinal":5},{"id":"zr-17724-sub-aff769a9c2495948","label":"4.80","sourceAnchor":null,"plainText":"4.80","ordinal":6},{"id":"zr-17724-s